From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nico Burns <nico.burns@cognition.ai>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop scroll chaining at overscroll-behavior: contain and none

Stylo already computes `overscroll-behavior`, but `BaseDocument::scroll`
chained whatever a scroller couldn't consume regardless, so `contain` and
`none` behaved like `auto`. Zero the remainder on an axis whose value is
`contain` or `none` (they behave the same, as Blitz draws no overscroll
effect). It applies to scroll containers only; the viewport takes the
root element's value, and text inputs, which scroll their own content,
honour it too.

A wheel's notches (`scroll_chain_smoothly`, from the previous patch) walk
the chain to the first scroller that can move; they stop at a contained
axis the same way.

Ported from blitz#1636 (fixes blitz#1629) onto the pinned revision, with
the tests from blitz#1631 and one for a wheel's notch.
